[Event "Knight School"]
[Opening "Center Game"]
[Variation "Danish Gambit Declined: Sorensen Defense"]
[ECO "C21"]
[Character "solid,positional"]
[Risk "medium"]
[EarlyMate "white"]
[Tricks "pawn-grab"]
[Themes "give-back-the-pawn,centre-pawns"]
[For "black"]
[Kind "gambit"]
[Opponent "2.d4 exd4 3.c3"]
[Start "1. e4 e5"]

2. d4 { Opens the centre at once so White's pieces get open lines early. } 2... exd4 { Takes the pawn. White cannot win it back quickly without losing time. } 3. c3 { Offers the pawn on d4 back: if Black takes, White gets a big lead in development in return. } 3... d5 { The key reply. It hits e4 at once and returns a pawn on Black's terms. Grabbing everything with ...dxc3 gives White a strong attack. } 4. exd5 { Takes the pawn and opens the e-file. White is a pawn up for a moment but Black can win it back. } ( 4. cxd4 dxe4 5. Nc3 Nf6 ) ( 4. Qxd4 Nf6 5. exd5 Qxd5 ) ( 4. e5 c5 5. cxd4 Nc6 ) 4... Qxd5 { Gets the pawn back, and the queen eyes both d4 and g2. } 5. cxd4 { Takes the pawn back and White now has a centre pawn on d4. The queen on d5 can be hit by a knight on c3 later. } ( 5. Nf3 Nc6 6. cxd4 Bb4+ ) 5... Nc6 { Develops and attacks d4. } 6. Nf3 { Develops and defends d4 once more. } 6... Bb4+ 7. Nc3 Bg4 8. Be2 ( 8. Bd2 Bxc3 9. Bxc3 Bxf3 ) 8... Bxf3 { Takes the knight that guards d4. } 9. Bxf3 Qc4 10. Bxc6+ ( 10. Qb3 Qxb3 11. axb3 Nge7 ) 10... bxc6 11. Qe2+ Qxe2+ 12. Kxe2 O-O-O { Queens are off, White's king is stuck in the middle, and Black's pieces are ready. Plan: ...Nf6, ...Rhe8 and pressure on the isolated d4 pawn. } *
